{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFiled from the escape analysis on marshy-chummy-coot (2399-5e49-6b28-4d59). The silently-inert primary dedup guard (bug aa7b, origin 789c) left an invariant violation visible in committed production state for the feature's entire life: `.bridge_state/bindings.json` showed `comment_ids == 0` while bindings grew past 2,475 and outbound comment posts kept succeeding. No layer read that signal. This ticket adds the layer that reads it.\n\nDESIGN DECISION (operator-ratified 2026-08-22, recorded as a ticket comment): every successfully posted outbound Jira comment must have its returned comment ID recorded locally; divergence (post succeeded, local `comment_ids` unchanged) raises a bridge alert. Alert firing is DEBOUNCED ACROSS 2 CONSECUTIVE RECONCILE PASSES — it fires only when the same divergence is observed in 2 consecutive passes, matching the N-of-M alarm philosophy of the voter-observability lane. Not per-pass immediate firing. This adjudicates the first original acceptance criterion.\n\n## Approach\nIn-process, operation-linked (no CI trigger — runs wherever the reconciler runs, satisfying `project.portability` by construction), reusing seams that already exist:\n\n1. **Count successful posts at the shared enactment seam.** Both outbound comment enactment sites — `create_one` (dispatch_one.py:389-393) and `_update_one_dispatch_comments` (dispatch_apply_phases.py:386-390) — already call the shared `_record_comment_id(binding_store, entry, result)` (dispatch_apply_phases.py:311) immediately after a successful `add_comment` return. Add a guarded `note_comment_posted()` call there BEFORE its recording guards, so every successful post is tallied even when recording no-ops (the exact failure class this invariant watches).\n2. **Counters live on the `BindingStore` facade** (binding_store.py:121): per-pass posted counter (`note_comment_posted` / `comment_posts_this_pass`), `comment_ids_count()` (len of the `comment_ids` map owned by `BindingLifecycle.record_comment_id`, binding_lifecycle.py:484), and a baseline `comment_ids` count captured at construction. The store is constructed once per pass in `_load_snapshots`, so \"gained this pass\" = count now − count at load.\n3. **Pure debounce step in `invariants.py`** (the established invariants home, cf. `detect_at_most_one_local_id`): `step_comment_divergence(prev_consecutive, divergent) -> (new_consecutive, fire)` — a healthy observation (no posts, or posts with map growth) resets the counter to 0; a divergent observation increments it; fire only when the count reaches 2. Directly unit-testable, no I/O.\n4. **IO check `check_comment_id_recording(binding_store, repo_root, pass_id)` in `invariants.py`**: reads posted/gained off the store, loads the cross-pass counter from `bridge_state/comment_id_divergence.json` (local scratch, same residency as `bridge_state/bridge_alerts`; corrupt/absent state fails open to 0), runs the pure step, persists the new state, and on fire appends a record through the existing sibling `alert_store` (`append`/`is_deduped`, 24h dedup key `bridge-alert:comment-id-divergence`) whose message names the invariant and the pass.\n5. **End-of-pass hook**: one fail-open `try/except` call to `ctx.invariants_mod.check_comment_id_recording(...)` inside `_persist_and_log`'s persist branch (reconcile.py:613; `ctx.invariants_mod` is already loaded at reconcile.py:250). Runs once per pass, after the binding-store save, skipped in no-write mode.\n\nreconcile.py is at 799 LOC against the 800 hard cap, so `_write_prev_snapshot_key_set` (reconcile.py:607, no references outside reconcile.py) moves to `reconcile_helpers.py` along the existing re-export seam (reconcile.py:59-63 already loads `_helpers` and re-binds names), keeping the module under the cap.\n\nRiskiest assumption: both enactment sites reach `_record_comment_id` on every successful post — confirmed by reading dispatch_one.py:389-393 and dispatch_apply_phases.py:386-390 (the call is unconditional on the success path); the RED test for scenario (b) exercises the counting seam first, before the debounce plumbing is built on it.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py` — posted counter + `comment_ids_count()` + at-load baseline on the facade\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py` — count the post in `_record_comment_id` before the recording guards\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/invariants.py` — pure debounce step + `check_comment_id_recording` (state file + alert append)\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py` — fail-open end-of-pass call in `_persist_and_log`; move `_write_prev_snapshot_key_set` out\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py` — receives `_write_prev_snapshot_key_set`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_comment_id_divergence_invariant.py` — new (RED-first)\n\n## Testing\nRED-first hermetic unit tests over a tmp tracker dir (no Jira, no network; the `spec_from_file_location` loader convention of test_binding_store_comment_ids.py):\n- (a) divergence observed once (posted>0, comment_ids gained none) → counter=1, NO alert record in `bridge_state/bridge_alerts/*.jsonl`\n- (b) same divergence in 2 consecutive passes → alert record present; its message names the invariant and the pass_id\n- (c) divergence in pass 1, healthy pass 2 (recording works), divergence in pass 3 → counter reset between, NO alert\n- healthy pass (posts recorded) and idle pass (no posts) → no alert, counter stays 0\n- pure-step table test for `step_comment_divergence`\n- `_record_comment_id` counts a successful post even when the entry carries no `local_comment_key` (recording no-ops, the post still tallies)\n- corrupt state file → fails open to counter 0, pass does not raise\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The pure debounce step fires only on the 2nd consecutive divergent observation and a healthy observation resets the counter; checked by the pure-step unit test passing\n- [ ] Every successful outbound comment post is tallied at the shared `_record_comment_id` seam independent of whether recording succeeds; checked by the no-`local_comment_key` unit test passing\n- [ ] A divergent pass followed by a second divergent pass appends a `bridge_alerts` JSONL record (deduped via `alert_store.is_deduped`) whose message names the invariant and the pass; checked by scenario-(b) unit test asserting the record's key, pass_id and message\n- [ ] One divergent pass alone, and a divergence resolved between passes, produce NO alert; checked by scenario-(a)/(c) unit tests passing\n- [ ] Cross-pass debounce state lives in `bridge_state/comment_id_divergence.json` and a corrupt/absent file fails open to 0 without breaking the pass; checked by the corrupt-state unit test passing\n- [ ] `make lint` (ruff + format + complexity ratchet `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`), `make typecheck`, and the targeted reconciler test selection pass; every `src/rebar` file stays ≤800 LOC (module-size gate); checked by the commands exiting 0 in-session\n\n## Non-goals\nNo new review criterion, no CI-coupled trigger (ci-gate-compat is rejected precedent), no change to the dedup guard itself (fixed in 8d98c298fa8), no bug auto-filing from this alert (the at-most-one invariant's filing sink is not extended to it)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787438835009941001,"uuid":"74e4aa84-233a-4307-b2c2-4c5b5d402bf9"}